      "id": "9fa6a120-8ea5-4f49-96c4-848bcce2afd0",
      "type": "event",
      "date": "2026-04-08T14:06:00.000Z",
      "title": "Lupin Limited Announces Approval of Dapagliflozin and Metformin Hydrochloride Extended-Release Tablets in the United States",
      "body": "Lupin Limited announced that it has received approval from the United States Food and Drug Administration for its Abbreviated New Drug Application for Dapagliflozin and Metformin Hydrochloride Extended-Release Tablets, 5 mg/500 mg, 5 mg/1,000 mg, 10 mg/500 mg, 10 mg/1,000 mg. The company also received tentative approval for Dapagliflozin and Metformin Hydrochloride Extended-Release Tablets, 2.5 mg/1,000 mg. The United States Food and Drug Administration has approved Lupin's Dapagliflozin and Metformin Hydrochloride Extended-Release Tablets as bioequivalent to Xigduo XR for the indications in the approved labeling.",
      "keyDevTypeId": "41",
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "EventActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "78eb4854-02cd-4407-a696-adb86a6e96e8",
      "type": "event",
      "date": "2026-03-31T13:11:00.000Z",
      "title": "Lupin Limited Receives Tentative Approval from U.S. Fda for Sugammadex Injection",
      "body": "Lupin Limited announced that it has received tentative approval from the United States Food and Drug Administration (U.S. FDA) for its Abbreviated New Drug Application for Sugammadex Injection, 200 mg/2 mL (100 mg/mL) and 500 mg/5 mL (100 mg/mL) Single-Dose Vial. Lupin's Sugammadex Injection, 200 mg/2 mL (100 mg/mL) and 500 mg/5 mL (100 mg/mL) Single-Dose Vial is bioequivalent to Merck's Bridion Injection and indicated for the reversal of neuromuscular blockade induced by rocuronium bromide and vecuronium bromide in adults and pediatric patients aged 2 years and older undergoing surgery.",
      "keyDevTypeId": "41",
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "EventActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "0ba9bfd6-ea4e-46a1-9efc-5eea9bace5a5",
      "type": "event",
      "date": "2026-03-25T03:43:00.000Z",
      "title": "Lupin Limited Receives Tentative Approval From U.S. FDA For Pitolisant Tablets",
      "body": "Lupin Limited announced that it has received tentative approval from the United States Food and Drug Administration for its Abbreviated New Drug Application for Pitolisant Tablets, 4.45mg and 17.8mg. This product would be manufactured at Lupin’s Nagpur facility in India. The United States Food and Drug Administration has tentatively approved Lupin’s Pitolisant Tablets 4.45mg and 17.8 mg as bioequivalent to Wakix for the indication in the approved labeling.",
      "keyDevTypeId": "41",
      "source_url": null,
