      "title": "Third quarter 2026 earnings: Revenues exceed analysts expectations while EPS lags behind",
      "body": "Third quarter 2026 results: EPS: ₹25.74 (up from ₹18.75 in 3Q 2025). Revenue: ₹71.7b (up 24% from 3Q 2025). Net income: ₹11.8b (up 38% from 3Q 2025). Profit margin: 16% (up from 15% in 3Q 2025). The increase in margin was driven by higher revenue. Revenue exceeded analyst estimates by 5.8%. Earnings per share (EPS) missed analyst estimates by 9.1%. Revenue is forecast to grow 4.7% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 10% growth forecast for the Pharmaceuticals industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 64% per year but the company’s share price has only increased by 49% per year, which means it is significantly lagging earnings growth.",
